    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>London was founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> about 47 CE and was destroyed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boudica">Boudica</a>'s Iceni within about fifteen years, then rebuilt as a planned town.</li><li>After a post-Roman decline it revived inside its old walls from 886, and from 1066 it was the place where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s kings were crowned and where government settled at Westminster.</li><li>Plague in 1665 and 1666 and the Great Fire of 1666 struck the old city, and from the 19th century it grew into the world's largest city, with 6.7 million people in 1900.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1666 the Great Fire destroyed about 60 per cent of London, including 87 parish churches, yet it is believed to have cost at most 16 lives.</p></aside>
    </section>

